WF-04 — Account Standing, Contribution Accuracy and Reputation
Part A defines three independent, displayable measures and their reviewed outcomes. Part B defines event eligibility, score history, accuracy evidence, APIs, concurrency and recovery. WF-01 through Admin Portal use contract baseline AMVN-BE-2026-11-14-r2; owning Part B contracts govern implementation details. Diagram references are supporting views, outside this text-only freeze.
Contract baseline: AMVN-BE-2026-11-14-r2. Freeze scope: WF-01 through Admin Portal; implementation follows the owning Part B and shared bindings.
Implementation lookup: shared sources and entities B.0–B.1; ordered credit/window/snapshot B.2; endpoints/ranking B.3; guards/concurrency B.4; baseline versus deferred policy B.5; jobs/audit B.6; errors B.7; acceptance B.8. WF1 B.15 owns publication-time source classification; WF4 alone applies eligible credit.
Part A — Technical / Design Specification
A.1 Purpose and ownership
WF-04 owns AccountStandingScore (conduct and participation, 0–100), ContributionAccuracyRate (raw correct/(correct+incorrect), nullable) and ReputationPoints (non-spendable ranking points). No measure is derived from another. WF-01 owns claim evidence, assessment and publication; WF-02 owns reports, votes and community review. Account standing controls participation, claim accuracy supports evidence weighting, and reputation controls ranking only. AI confidence and Admin approval authority are not increased by standing or ranking. No wallet, exchange, reward catalogue or redemption is introduced.
A.2 Actors and authorization
Guest may search and view published place information without an account. Guest cannot contribute, vote, report or use private reputation history. User is an active signed-in account with isAdmin=false and may contribute, view the contributor leaderboard and read their own reputation/status. Contributor and Accessibility Seeker are usage descriptions of User. Admin has isAdmin=true, signs in only through ReactJS Admin Portal and cannot use the mobile login or ordinary User write session. Admin reviews source-backed typed standing/reputation adjustments under B.3. All protected endpoints recheck current account state, isAdmin, session/revocation, ownership and endpoint authorization under WF-01 A.2.3. Registration cannot set isAdmin; there is no Role/UserRole schema. Apply WF-01 B.0.13 JWT/current-session authorization and the same human/Worker credential separation.
A.3 Reputation pipeline
An authorized publication, claim assessment, report resolution or confirmed conduct decision commits a durable ContributionEvent with its source transaction. API-side processing atomically applies accuracy transitions and/or typed UserScoreHistory entries, updates UserContributionStats, completes the event and writes NotificationOutbox. One event may affect both standing and reputation; accuracy is derived from assessed facts, never a percentage delta. Retry cannot duplicate any effect. Raw upload/vote/report volume, an AI failure or an unresolved allegation grants neither credit nor penalty. Naming: ContributionEvent is the current renamed ReputationEvent; retain one event authority, not parallel event tables. Publication source persistence is atomic with Published/feature/history, while credit application is a later distinct WF4 transaction. Exact source/effect uniqueness and locked completion prevent duplicate histories/counters on retry.
A.4 User actions and outcomes
Users see standing, contribution accuracy with correct/assessed claim counts, reputation, rank and owned source outcomes. Reports and comments are excluded from ContributionAccuracyRate; do not expose a separate report-accuracy score. With zero assessed claims, accuracy is null and displayed as 'Chưa đủ dữ liệu', not 0%. The B.3 held-event queue/detail/review endpoints accept authorized investigation references without adding a ticket subsystem. Pending and HeldForReview events have no applied effects; Credited means all applicable metric effects committed, including counter-only or negative effects; Cancelled means no applicable effect. These technical event states do not imply every event is a positive award.
A.5 Reputation and ranking lifecycle
A.5.1 Eligible credit
Eligible first-place publication earns +2 AccountStanding and +5 ReputationPoints; an eligible enrichment earns +2 AccountStanding and +2 ReputationPoints. Apply each at most once per qualifying submission, not per media/claim. The existing 30-day repeat guard also prevents repeat positive standing awards. Publication source classification remains first actual publisher, not Location creator. Raw claim accuracy is evaluated independently of reward eligibility.
Repeated contributions can still improve published information while being ineligible for another award. WF1 B.15 owns source classification; B.2 below owns the same-user/place/scope/feature guard, source ordering and credit application.
A.5.2 Authoritative score
AccountStandingScore starts at 50: newScore=clamp(currentScore+requestedDelta,0,100); no surplus above 100 is banked. Store requestedDelta, appliedDelta=newScore-currentScore and balances. ContributionAccuracyRate=C/(C+W), null when C+W=0; no smoothing and no +/− percentage transactions. ContributionAccuracyRate measures assessed contribution claims only. Report and comment outcomes never enter its numerator or denominator, including valid reports and confirmed comment violations. ReputationPoints starts at 0 and equals retained legitimate ranking awards minus source-linked revocations. It has no upper cap, spending or automatic time decay. Example: eligible new-place and enrichment awards give standing 54 and reputation 7; accuracy depends on their separately assessed claims. Display examples: 'Uy tín tài khoản: 82/100'; 'Độ tin cậy: 90% · 45/50 nhận định đã kiểm chứng'; 'Danh vọng: 1.250 điểm · Hạng 18'. A 90% observed accuracy rate is not a calibrated 90% probability for the next claim. Define C/W as distinct current ConfirmedCorrect/ConfirmedIncorrect contribution observations. Exclude pending, Unknown, Inconclusive, reports, comments and votes. Display 100×C/(C+W) rounded to one decimal; compute with full precision, null when no observations. Revision subtracts the old outcome indicator and adds the new under source/account locks. A later physical change never makes an originally correct claim wrong. History support H=min((C+W)/10,1) adjusts aggregation weight, not the displayed raw ratio.
A.5.3 Leaderboard and badges
Rank active non-Admin Users with positive ReputationPoints and a retained eligible award by ReputationPoints DESC, DistinctCreditedLocationCount DESC, ReputationReachedAt ASC NULLS LAST, UserId ASC. Report-only qualifying contributors may rank with distinct-location count zero. A report award does not fabricate a credited publication Location. Public board fields are displayName, rank, rankBadge and ReputationPoints. Standing, accuracy denominators, private history and investigation details remain on the owner/Admin views.
Let N count the qualified users defined in A.5.3. LeaderboardDisplayLimit=min(50,max(10,10×floor(N/100))). N<200 gives Top 10, then Top 20/30/40 for 200/300/400, and Top 50 for N>=500; return fewer if fewer qualify. Rank badges follow current position, grant no points, standing, confidence, permissions or publication advantage, and are not permanently persisted.
The owner's private rankLabel is exact #1–#500, 500+ for #501–#1,000, 1000+ above #1,000, or Unranked without a qualifying contribution. Do not expose an exact private rank above 500. Public positions remain exact only within LeaderboardDisplayLimit. The API supplies displayLimit and badge labels; clients do not hardcode the growth thresholds.
A.6 Scope boundary
Scope includes independent standing, contribution-only accuracy, non-spendable reputation, source audit and contributor ranking. Normal standing is 40–100, Limited 20–39, Restricted 0–19. Existing account suspension is a separate authorized decision and may apply at any score. Restricted accounts retain public reads, owned status, support and a bounded path to valid contribution. No automatic permanent ban, spending, tier multiplier or automatic publication is enabled.
A.7 Reviewed adjustments and misconduct
Event catalogue v3-metrics-3: qualifying new-place publication +2 standing/+5 reputation; qualifying enrichment +2/+2; earliest novel confirmed useful factual place/feature/submission report +1/+1 once per issue. Comment and DuplicateLocation reports grant no reward. Confirmed attributable false contribution −4 standing once per offending act; deliberate fabrication −6 replaces −4. Confirmed malicious reporting −4; rejected or honestly mistaken reports alone have no penalty. Confirmed comment categories: SpamAdvertising −2; HarassmentHate −4; PrivacyThreat −6; CoordinatedManipulation −6; Other warning/hide only until a separately approved category exists. Coordinated vote manipulation −6. For one incident apply the highest applicable sanction once, not stacked categories/report counts; distinct repeated acts need separate reviewed evidence. Each sanction requires uninvolved Admin, actual evidence, reason, category, ViolationKey and policy. Routine hiding, AI suspicion, report volume, service errors or later physical changes never prove misconduct. Comment/report conduct changes standing only, not reputation, claim accuracy or confidence. An overturned sanction compensates the previously applied delta once; severity revision first compensates the old sanction then applies the replacement. Invalid contribution awards may be separately source-revoked, never charged as an unlinked reputation fine.
A.8 Notifications and privacy
Use the existing NotificationOutbox. Score notifications use sourceType=UserScoreHistory with sourceId/sourceEventId=history.Id; counter-only outcome notifications use ContributionEvent.Id. Commit safe owner-only notification metadata with the applied effects, reuse identities on retry and never expose allegations or evidence on Guest projections. An outbox failure cannot roll back a committed outcome or cause another award.
A.9 End-to-end sequence
Authorized source decision → durable ContributionEvent → API-side source/version and reward eligibility checks → atomic typed history, accuracy projection, stats and event completion → notification delivery. Positive award ineligibility does not prevent legitimate claim assessment or publication. A recovered/replayed event returns its stored result without changing counters, balances or timestamps again.
A.10 Error and fallback cases
Missing/unsupported PolicyVersion blocks source application for investigation. Duplicate source replay returns its existing outcome; changed payload with the same idempotency key returns 409. Concurrent eligible sources serialize under the account lock and recheck the feature guard. Unavailable authoritative metrics in WF-02 yields PendingValidation with zero weight, not invented default accuracy. Unauthorized/private reads return 401/403 under the shared contract. Missing adjustment authority/reason/source or self-adjustment is rejected without ledger writes. A worker crash leaves a recoverable source with no partial ledger/snapshot credit.
A.11 Acceptance outcomes
Acceptance: initial standing=50, reputation=0, contribution accuracy=null. Eligible new-place plus enrichment produces standing=54 and reputation=7; two independently confirmed correct claims produce accuracy=100% (2/2). Publication requires Admin approval at every score. Raw reports, rejected evidence and AI errors have no automatic penalty. Changed real-world conditions preserve earlier correct-at-observation assessments. Board size and private rank buckets remain as defined in A.5.3.
A.12 Baseline settings and deferred policies
Policy v3-metrics-3 unifies three independent measures, calibrated evidence weights, sanctions and participation limits. Retain historic versions/score histories and completed confidence snapshots. Deferred capabilities live in Optional and are excluded from current acceptance; deployment configuration is explicit, not an unresolved business rule. Shared formulas v3-metrics-3: T=C/(C+W), H=min((C+W)/10,1), R=2^(−max(0,ageDays)/180), w=T×H×R. Zero history gives zero weight; displayed T is never smoothed. WF1 uses one other contributor's latest comparable assessed published claim; WF2 uses one current eligible independent vote per contributor/version. Agreement=sum(w agreeing)/sum(w), null for zero total. EvidenceStrength=min(sum(w)/3,1), beta=.40×EvidenceStrength, FinalConfidence=(1−beta)×AIConfidence+beta×Agreement when AI and community are available. Zero total uses AIOnly; no content-based AI gives null/Unavailable. Standing/reputation never enter weights or confidence. Freeze evaluation time/source decisions/counters before calculation; exclude current author and prospective effects; never rewrite completed snapshots.
Part B — Implementation Specification
B.0 Authority and migration
Create the shared User/auth, IdempotencyRecord and NotificationOutbox once, then USER_CONTRIBUTION_STATS, USER_SCORE_HISTORY, CONTRIBUTION_EVENT and CLAIM_ASSESSMENT as the final scoring schema. No Reputation/Ledger/Snapshot compatibility tables, LifetimeTrustNet migration or separate ManualAdjustmentAudit are generated. UUID keys, UTC timestamptz, explicit concurrency/unique/checks and restrictive source/audit FKs are mandatory. Initial stats50 standing/0 ranking/no assessed accuracy are created with each account. Events/assessments and immutable typed history supply rebuild/reconciliation within this new system; never infer accuracy from Published or AI confidence.
Cross-workflow implementation baseline: create this module within the new .NET8 Code First solution under WF1 B.0.3–B.0.13. Use the shared defined User/auth, DbContext, repository/UoW, storage, jobs and outbox once; there is no old solution or backfill. Apply Worker→Internal Job API, typed DTOs, configuration, DI, generic bases, scoped IUnitOfWork facade and executable acceptance. The owning Part B defines business policies, routes, final schema and retry budgets. Scenario IDs replace diagram-pair numbering. All SQL/EF business access is API-side; scheduler storage is separately credentialed. Include the module in S01–S08 checkpointed generation and the complete test matrix.
B.1 Entities and invariants
ContributionEvent: Id uuid PK; UserId uuid FK; Type; Status; SourceDecisionVersion; IdempotencyKey unique; PolicyVersion; Reason; EligibilitySnapshot jsonb; CreatedAt; CreditedAt nullable. Retain nullable typed FKs SubmissionId, LocationId, ClaimAssessmentId, ReportStatusHistoryId, CommentModerationHistoryId and ReversedEventId as applicable; enforce event-type-specific required source, ownership and consistent target. Publication events require SubmissionId and LocationId, unique SubmissionId WHERE Type IN (NewLocationPublished,ExistingLocationEnriched), and unique LocationId WHERE Type=NewLocationPublished. Other event types are ClaimAssessmentFinalized, ClaimAssessmentRevised, ReportResolved, AccountViolationConfirmed, AccountViolationReversed, RewardRevoked and RewardRestored. Comment conduct events reference ReportStatusHistoryId for a Comment-target report or CommentModerationHistoryId for direct Admin moderation, with the target comment/version and violation identity. A confirmed comment violation produces only an AccountStanding history entry; no ranking or accuracy effect. Reviewed conduct outside an existing source decision stores immutable AdminId, reason and evidence references on its event. NominalReputationPoints is an audit hint, never proof of applied credit. Preserve HeldForReview review authority/deadline and eligibility snapshots.
Final held-event review contract: ContributionEvent adds Version bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT1 CHECK>0 and ReviewContext jsonb NULL. Increment Version on every committed event-state, active-hold or review decision change; source-event creation starts at1. The stored version guards release, credit, cancellation and reconciliation races. HeldForReview requires ReviewContext under a versioned schema containing holdReasonCode,heldAt,reviewDueAt,sourceDecisionVersion,authority="Wf04.Adjust" and append-only decisions[]. Initial HoldReviewDeadlineHours=48; deadline expiry marks the held item overdue for operations, never grants/cancels effects or resets source order. Keep the original hold and every review decision; no ticket, second ledger or separate scoring policy is created.
GET /api/v1/admin/contribution-events?status=HeldForReview&cursor&limit and GET /api/v1/admin/contribution-events/{eventId} require current AdminPortal/Wf04.Adjust and return authorized typed source/reason/version/deadline and safe evidence references. Default limit20,max100; order CreatedAt ASC,Id ASC with filter-bound opaque cursor. POST /api/v1/admin/contribution-events/{eventId}/review accepts {decision:Release|Cancel,expectedVersion,reason,evidenceRefs}, UUID Idempotency-Key and a current uninvolved Admin. Reason is trimmed10..1500; evidenceRefs is a nonempty bounded set of real authorized source references. Recheck conflict-of-interest against subject and all involved source contributors/reviewers under source→account→event locks. Authorized matching replay precedes mutable guards; stale409 EVENT_VERSION_CHANGED, non-held/unsupported transition409 INVALID_EVENT_TRANSITION, invalid source422, no rights401/403. Return200 {eventId,status,version,reviewedAt}.
Release appends the server-attributed review and changes HeldForReview→Pending, incrementing Version and committing replay/outbox together; dispatch processing after commit. It authorizes reevaluation only, never overrides source validity, predecessor ordering, typed policy/eligibility or creates an award in the review transaction. Missing/unresolved prerequisites return409 SOURCE_NOT_READY and retain the hold; dependency outage503. Cancel is allowed only for an unapplied positive publication/report award source with a reviewed ineligible/duplicate/withdrawn outcome; set Cancelled with reason and no score effect. Claim-assessment, conduct and compensation events cannot be cancelled here: revise the owning source decision or resolve its prerequisite, then process its ordered zero/nonzero effect normally. A completed Credited event never moves back to HeldForReview; inconsistencies use a source-linked correction/reversal event, preserving applied history. Re-holding a released Pending event for a genuinely changed source creates a new active hold instance in ReviewContext and preserves prior decisions; replay cannot extend a deadline.
Only the owning source/API processing service may enter HeldForReview with a real documented prerequisite/conflict reason. AI warnings, unusual volume, elapsed time and client requests alone are not misconduct. Test self-review denial, release without source readiness, cancelled publication/report reward without blocking legitimate accuracy, forbidden cancellation of assessment/compensation, concurrent Admin decisions, overdue/no automatic effect and predecessor recovery. One finalized source/version/effect is processed once; a scoring event must reference a real typed source or an explicitly authorized conduct decision, not only an unchecked polymorphic UUID. ContributionRewardGranted names the committed award outcome of an eligible NewLocationPublished/ExistingLocationEnriched event (or qualified report); publish that downstream outcome once using the original event identity. It is not a second input event that awards the same points again. Conduct events persist ViolationKey and confirmed category; enforce UNIQUE(UserId,ViolationKey,SourceDecisionVersion,Type) for conduct decisions and serialize current sanction selection by User/ViolationKey. Multiple report/direct-moderation routes reference the same incident key. Revision compensates the prior effective sanction before replacement and retains all history. Use exactly one authoritative decision FK, with optional correlated references; the reported comment author cannot be supplied by the client. Comment/DuplicateLocation ReportResolved bypasses positive-report awards. Only ClaimAssessmentFinalized/Revised changes accuracy counters.
Final accuracy application and rebuild contract: assessment authority and score application are separate commit boundaries. ContributionEvent.ClaimAssessmentId is the existing restrictive source FK; enforce UNIQUE(ClaimAssessmentId) WHERE Type IN (ClaimAssessmentFinalized,ClaimAssessmentRevised). Do not add another assessment-effect table. The source transaction appends assessment/supersession plus its Pending event; IsCurrent identifies the latest authoritative decision, not proof that its counter effect was applied.
For a counted observation, the effective applied outcome is the last source-ordered assessment in that observation's supersession chain whose unique accuracy event is Credited. A newer Pending/HeldForReview decision does not erase that applied predecessor. An uncounted correction never replaces a counted observation's applied outcome. Process each observation's assessment events in supersession order under source/account locks; an unapplied required predecessor blocks its successor. Derive old/new increments from immutable original/superseding outcomes and CountsTowardAccuracy, never from the current IsCurrent filter alone. Inconclusive contributes neither correct nor incorrect count. Freeze {previousAppliedAssessmentId,assessmentId,observationKey,oldOutcome,newOutcome,correctDelta,incorrectDelta,statsVersionBefore,statsVersionAfter} in the event's existing EligibilitySnapshot.accuracyEffect. Apply counters, increment stats/event versions, mark the event Credited and set CreditedAt atomically; authorized replay changes nothing. CreditedAt is the server completion time for every applied event, including counter-only, negative and clamped-zero effects, not only a positive reward.
Reputation-reconcile rebuilds counters from this same processed effective set, grouped by SubjectUserId/ObservationKey, in one consistent snapshot under the owning canonical source/account locks. It neither counts a Pending/Held assessment nor marks its event applied as a side effect of rebuild. Serialize rebuild with normal application so a later worker cannot apply a delta already included in the rebuilt projection. Rebuild standing/reputation from their ordered committed typed histories as before; preserve event source/decision history and cache invalidation. Evidence-weight readers use only this processed assessment/counter snapshot with its policy/version; they do not combine a pending revised verdict with pre-revision counters. Completed AI/community snapshots remain immutable. Tests cover Correct→Incorrect revision with delayed processing, two pending revisions, held predecessor, rebuild before/after application, concurrent rebuild/credit, uncounted correction and exact replay without negative/double counters.
