No spendable-account, point-lot, offer, code-inventory, redemption, debit or redemption-restriction entity belongs to this target schema. Do not add a replacement reward catalogue under another name.
B.2 Event and reputation contract
In one short API transaction, acquire canonical Location/source/issue locks when applicable before the affected account, recheck source revision and policy, and apply the applicable assessment transition plus at most one positive standing/reputation award per qualified source. Publication eligibility retains B.2's 30-day guard; report novelty uses canonical issue uniqueness. Both typed history entries, accuracy counts, stats version, event completion, replay response and outbox commit or roll back together. Counter-only/negative events also complete as Credited (processed), not as a positive reward. A no-effect ineligible award is Cancelled. Unresolved cases stay Pending/HeldForReview; no guessed default metrics. Prior source dependencies block out-of-order revisions until their predecessors are processed.
Use the publication source type established by WF1 B.15. The 30-day guard uses immutable Submission.PublishedAt in UTC, never event CreatedAt, processing time or CreditedAt. For each candidate selected published feature, compare earlier credited feature eligibility whose PublishedAt is strictly later than candidate.PublishedAt−30 days and precedes the candidate in event order; a separation of exactly 30×24 hours is eligible. Order sources by PublishedAt then SubmissionId; at equal timestamps the earlier ID is prior and participates in the guard. Record exactly which scoped features qualified, publication timestamps, prior source IDs, window bounds and policy in ContributionEvent.EligibilitySnapshot under WF1 B.3.13; keep Reason a bounded summary; one multi-feature enrichment credits at most +2. A feature blocked in an earlier partly credited submission does not gain a new guard timestamp from that submission.
Process pending sources in this event-time order for each affected account/canonical scope-feature; a later conflicting source waits if an earlier source is unresolved or HeldForReview. Reconciliation resolves all earlier committed publication sources before application, so late worker delivery cannot reorder eligibility. If an already-applied result is found inconsistent because of a discovered inconsistent source, retain that event as Credited and reconcile through its authorized source-linked correction/reversal event; do not move applied history back to HeldForReview, rewrite immutable ledger entries or apply a second award. NewLocationPublished remains subject to first-publication uniqueness and records its selected credited features for subsequent guards. Preserve eligibility policy, considered prior source IDs, window boundaries and outcome in EligibilitySnapshot for replay.
ReputationAwarded is nullable applied ranking points for a publication: null pending, zero final ineligible, +5/+2 after commit; it is not standing or accuracy. Expose standingDelta separately if applicable. ContributionEvent.NominalReputationPoints is nominal only. GET never initiates effects, and a submission cannot use its own prospective award or assessment to increase its verification weight.
B.3 Leaderboard and reputation API
GET /api/v1/leaderboard requires an active User session with isAdmin=false and returns up to LeaderboardDisplayLimit qualified Users: rank, rankBadge=Top{rank}, existing displayName, ReputationPoints and displayLimit. Keep Guest access limited to public place search/view; Guest private/account-reputation calls return 401. Filter candidates to active accounts with isAdmin=false, a retained qualifying publication or report award and positive ReputationPoints; historical Admin-owned rows do not enter the public board or qualified-user count. Order snapshots by ReputationPoints DESC, DistinctCreditedLocationCount DESC, ReputationReachedAt ASC NULLS LAST, UserId ASC. Read at most the first 1,000 qualified Users; their capped count yields the same displayLimit because it is already capped at 50 for N>=500. Reuse this bounded ordered set for board and private rankLabel; do not scan/persist rank for every User. Evaluate an appropriate B-tree ordering index with EXPLAIN ANALYZE as population grows; LIMIT alone does not guarantee an efficient sort.
GET /api/v1/me/reputation retains its route and returns accountStandingScore, contributionAccuracyRate nullable (0..1), correctClaimCount, incorrectClaimCount, reputationPoints, participationStatus, policyVersion, updatedAt, private rankLabel and derived rankBadge. History includes scoreType and source outcome. Display raw percentage plus assessed count; do not display smoothed values or treat zero history as 0% accurate.
POST /api/v1/admin/reputation-adjustments retains the existing route but requires userId, scoreType, action=ConfirmViolation|ReverseStandingEffect|RevokeReward|RestoreReward, reason, typed sourceEventId or originalHistoryEntryId, and amount only for bounded reward revocation/restoration. The server derives −2/−4/−6 from the reviewed A.7/B.5 violation category; no arbitrary standing amount or accuracy percentage is accepted. Require portal-scoped current Admin permission, Idempotency-Key and decision/version guard; forbid self/involved-source review. Return event/history/stats identities. Exact replay returns the original response; changed hash →409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED, invalid original source →422 INVALID_RESTORATION_REFERENCE, exhausted allowance →409 RESTORATION_LIMIT_EXCEEDED. All audit fields live in UserScoreHistory/ContributionEvent.
B.4 Validation and concurrency
Validate ownership, typed source FK, source version, reviewed evidence, policy, replay hash and original compensation reference. Acquire source/Location/issue locks before account, then referenced history consistently; recheck under lock. Multiple event workers and distinct adjustment keys cannot double-count an assessment, duplicate an award, bypass 30-day eligibility or over-restore a reward. Store ApplicationSequence under account lock. All score history, counts, stats, source completion and outbox are atomic; no network/AI/storage call occurs in the transaction. Exact replay is authorized before mutable-state checks. An ineligible reward never blocks a legitimate publication or assessed accuracy result.
B.5 Configuration and policy gates
PolicyVersion=v3-metrics-3. Configurable defaults: InitialStanding=50; NormalStandingMin=40; LimitedStandingMin=20; PublicationStandingDelta=2; ValidNovelFactualReportStandingDelta=1; AttributableFalseSubmissionPenalty=4; FabricationPenalty=6; MaliciousReportPenalty=4; CommentSpamPenalty=2; CommentHarassmentPenalty=4; CommentPrivacyThreatPenalty=6; ManipulationPenalty=6; NewLocationReputationPoints=5; EnrichmentReputationPoints=2; ValidNovelFactualReportReputationPoints=1. No reward for Comment or DuplicateLocation reports. AccuracyHistoryTarget=10; CommunityEvidenceTargetWeight=3; MaxCommunityShare=.40; ClaimHalfLifeDays=180; VoteHalfLifeDays=180. No smoothing of displayed accuracy, standing/reputation evidence multiplier, automatic decay, misconduct determination or publication.
Participation defaults: LimitWindow=UtcCalendarDay; NormalSubmissionLimit=5, LimitedSubmissionLimit=2, RestrictedSubmissionLimit=1; NormalReportLimit=5, LimitedReportLimit=2, RestrictedReportLimit=1. Count committed new initial submissions and reports per User/server UTC date; failures and exact authorized replays consume none. Resubmission uses MaxResubmissions=3 per stable Submission instead of another initial-submission quota, with no owner/Location/scope change. Comments keep 10/hour and votes10/10min; standing<20 requires new-vote validation. Check current band/quota atomically; exhaustion returns429 with reset/retry information. A lowered standing affects new writes immediately while public reads/owned status remain. Missing authoritative stats returns retryable unavailability, not invented defaults. Validate positive integer limits Normal>=Limited>=Restricted>0 and version all overrides; these are initial policy defaults for calibration. Suspension independently denies protected writes and is lifted only by authorized review.
B.6 Background work and audit
Durable Hangfire handlers call authenticated Internal Job API endpoints; they do not use the business database or repositories. ReputationCreditJob.ProcessEventAsync(eventId) calls InternalJobApiClient.CreditReputationAsync→ReputationJobsController→IReputationCreditService. The API-side service locks/rechecks Pending or eligible HeldForReview sources, consumes retained authorized review outcomes, rebuilds missing eligibility snapshots and commits ledger/score/event/outbox changes atomically. Reconciliation and outbox delivery use the shared maintenance API in WF-01 B.0.4. Monitor ordinary application within the initial 15-minute target; alert after 60 minutes unresolved and route held work through B.1/B.3's held-event review contract, with HoldReviewDeadlineHours=48 by default. These are operating targets, not promised credit times. Deadline expiry, unusual volume or AI warnings alone do not establish misconduct or change any metric. No new ticket/appeal, inventory, issuance or fulfillment job is introduced.
B.7 Error contract
401: Guest/private or missing authenticated User/portal session. 403: wrong isAdmin/session context, disabled account or unauthorized adjustment; User portal login and Admin mobile login are denied. 409: changed idempotent payload, conflicting current source/version or stale reviewed adjustment; exact replay returns the existing result. 422: malformed/unsupported source, UUID, units, policy reference or missing reason. Pending source/recovery failure does not fabricate credit or zero authoritative metrics. Notification failure retries without another ledger entry. Rate limits and account disablement follow the shared auth/rate-limit infrastructure defined in WF1.
B.8 Tests and Definition of Done
Verify Guest anonymous public place search/view and denial of contribution/report/account-private routes; User mobile access with isAdmin=false; Admin portal-only login with isAdmin=true; privilege injection rejection and immediate elevated-session invalidation after removal. Verify no Role/UserRole schema or removed exchange endpoint/schema/job remains.
Test initial 50/0/null; two qualifying publications yield standing54/reputation7 with accuracy based on actual claim decisions. Test 99+2 applies1; 100−4 gives96; no surplus banking. Test raw 1/1 and100/100 both display100% with different history support. Test 2 correct/1 incorrect mixed submission, no data=null, same-observation revision duplicates, duplicate reports, changed real-world conditions, current-assessment revision, pending/inconclusive/AI failure and votes/comments excluded from accuracy. Publication and report rewards apply once, do not repeat on retry/resubmit and remain independent of counter updates. Keep 30-day boundary/order/late-worker/merge tests; positive standing follows the same publication reward guard. Test canonical issue competition and report-only leaderboard entrants. QCVN comparison itself is not a score event or claim verdict: adding/changing a criterion snapshot never directly changes AccountStandingScore, ReputationPoints or accuracy counters. A later source-backed claim assessment or reviewed misconduct decision uses the existing WF4 event/reversal contract, without double-counting a measurement correction.
Keep leaderboard display-limit/private-rank boundary tests and deterministic ReputationPoints tie breakers. Standing and accuracy never change rank. Reward revocation/restoration changes retained reputation and eligible distinct publication count; conduct sanctions alone do not. Validate Normal/Limited/Restricted boundaries39/40 and19/20, configured 5/2/1 quotas and server UTC calendar-day boundaries, authorized idempotent replay, recovery and suspension precedence. Validate versioned defaults/overrides; test simultaneous quota writes, UTC reset, immediate band changes, correction allowance and suspension precedence.
Test all typed sources, self-review rejection, severity replacement without stacking −2/−4/−6, malicious versus honest report, comment conduct with standing-only impact and unchanged ReputationPoints/claim counters/confidence, linked award revocation and penalty, full standing reversal based on actual applied amount, waived capped remainder and no duplicate reversal. Reward fixture: original10, revoke10, restore6 then4, further1 fails; race6/6 permits at most one. Rebuild counters from the processed effective assessment set and rebuild scores from ordered committed histories under B.1/B.4; pending/held revisions remain unapplied. Preserve completed confidence snapshots and fault-inject before/after commit and notification delivery. Confidence fixtures: AI=.8/no evidence →.8 AIOnly; agreement1/strength.1 →.808; agreement1/strength1 →.88; agreement.25/strength1 →.58; missing AI →null and Admin review. Assert no source uses its own prospective metrics. Shared fixtures: C1/W0 gives accuracy1,H.1,weight.1 at age0; C100/W0 gives accuracy1,H1,weight1. Age180 halves each weight. C3/W1 gives accuracy.75,H.4,weight.3. AI.8 with three recent full-support agreeing contributors: total3,strength1,beta.4,final.88. One new contributor with one correct claim: weight.1,strength1/30,beta1/75,final .8026666667. No content-based AI branch (including GPS/quality-only input) gives null/Unavailable/manual review. Standing sanctions−2/−4/−6, malicious-report−4 and their reversals never affect reputation or claim accuracy. Every accepted analysis goes PendingModeration; only Admin requests supplementation.
